In article <1400@yenta.alb.nm.us> dt@yenta.alb.nm.us (David B. Thomas)
>proposes using the f key to toggle fighting mode and the #swim command
>to enter water.

This is not a perfect interface, but it would solve some problems.  In
real D&D a party would never accidentally walk into water, unless the
water was camaflouged or the party was mentally impaired.  (You should
be able to drown in nethack by moving in the wrong direction if you
are hallucinating or confused.  No confirmation there.)  Nor would a
real D&D party attack a monster by accidentally invading its space
(like, hey man, you're invading my space, quit it).

I am not suggesting that nethack be more like D&D in general, but I
would like it in this specific instance.

Drawbacks to having fight mode and move mode are that you might want
to alternate moving and fighting in a room full of monsters.  The interface
deserves some more thought.  I would let "f<dir>" mean fight for one turn
in direction <dir>.  "F" could toggle fighting mode.  "m<dir>" would allow
you to still move while in fighting mode.  Options should allow the user
to stick with the current interface or possibly some other interface.

